  "repair": "The Win32 driver retains its first result/error until actual child close and outstanding window-close calls finish. Abort retries WM_CLOSE then requests SIGKILL; refused/failed termination retains the operation and observers. Observed exit ends a separate worker lifetime; delayed binding preparation refuses window messages after that known exit. Graceful close retries continue after failed force termination and accept late showing. Window-close calls are serialized; observed exit stops new controls. Event subscriptions are removed at closure and native error causes remain retained.",
